WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.565 --> 00:00:15.548
For days Jo locked herself up in her sanctuary, telling everyone that she was working on a new

2
00:00:15.608 --> 00:00:19.650
novel, when in fact she was bawling her eyes out.

3
00:00:20.511 --> 00:00:25.653
She didn't fool anybody, because it was clear from her puffy red eyes and swollen nose that she

4
00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:27.114
hadn't spent the night writing.

5
00:00:27.955 --> 00:00:33.691
Having decided it was time to face reality, Mother gently knocked on the door, and said, "Jo?

6
00:00:34.051 --> 00:00:34.812
May I come in?"

7
00:00:34.832 --> 00:00:39.196
"Mmm Jo said in a muffled voice.

8
00:00:40.056 --> 00:00:44.580
Seeing Mother's kind, understanding eyes, Jo broke out in a new wave of tears.

9
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.405
"Shh, darling, just let it out," comforted Mother.

10
00:00:49.425 --> 00:00:54.069
"It's not fair," wept Jo.

11
00:00:54.089 --> 00:00:57.572
"She knew how much I wanted to travel to Europe.

12
00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:03.184
Every year she would make me believe that the next year I could come along, but now to

13
00:01:03.244 --> 00:01:06.806
choose Amy instead it's unbearable."

14
00:01:06.826 --> 00:01:12.650
"Do you remember how you used to feel when you came home each day from Aunt March's?"

15
00:01:13.131 --> 00:01:13.671
asked Mother.

16
00:01:14.492 --> 00:01:18.234
Sniffing, Jo replied, "Yes.

17
00:01:18.815 --> 00:01:20.276
She annoyed me to no end."

18
00:01:21.236 --> 00:01:26.000
"Now imagine if you had to spend all day and night with her for one year.

19
00:01:26.664 --> 00:01:29.145
Honestly, Jo, do you think you could manage that?"

20
00:01:29.465 --> 00:01:30.485
Mother reasoned with her.

21
00:01:31.585 --> 00:01:37.167
Wiping her nose with the back of her hand, Jo thought about it but did not answer, so

22
00:01:37.247 --> 00:01:42.709
Mother continued, "You once told me about the hundreds of libraries and museums you wanted to visit.

23
00:01:43.589 --> 00:01:46.750
Do you think Aunt March would allow you the freedom to do that?"

24
00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:52.351
Jo, who had stopped crying, shook her head and said, "I never thought about it that way.

25
00:01:53.472 --> 00:01:58.022
You're right, Mother, Aunt March would never let me follow my own personal dreams.

26
00:01:59.223 --> 00:02:02.385
Instead I would be at her beck and call every moment of the day."

27
00:02:03.346 --> 00:02:08.809
Patting Jo on the back, Mother said, "But Amy reacts differently as Aunt March rightly sees.

28
00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:14.073
Amy is quite happy going for tea, socializing, and taking strolls.

29
00:02:15.094 --> 00:02:18.456
That's why she would be a better companion on this particular trip.

30
00:02:19.256 --> 00:02:20.557
Do you understand that now?"

31
00:02:21.638 --> 00:02:24.160
Jo nodded heartily and said, "Yes, Mother.

32
00:02:24.776 --> 00:02:29.460
I'm still jealous that Amy is going to see Europe before me, but she deserves it.

33
00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:33.043
She is very good to Aunt March and to our neighbors."

34
00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:37.846
Jo told Mother how well behaved Amy had been when they made their calls.

35
00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:44.671
Remembering how hard her sister worked to please others reminded Jo of Amy's words on the road: "I

36
00:02:44.772 --> 00:02:49.675
still believe that good will come if we try to show kindness to others regardless of how they

37
00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:50.216
see us."

38
00:02:51.252 --> 00:02:55.795
Jo had to admit that she learned something quite valuable from her sister through this incident.

39
00:02:56.936 --> 00:03:01.339
In the girls' bedroom, Amy had a lot to do in preparation for her trip.

40
00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:06.923
"Aunt March says not to pack too many things since she will give me an allowance so I

41
00:03:06.963 --> 00:03:11.706
can get my dresses tailored in the European style," Amy said excitedly to Beth.

42
00:03:12.547 --> 00:03:14.928
"Europeans are so cultured and stylish.

43
00:03:15.569 --> 00:03:18.190
I think you're going to fit right in, Amy," said Beth.

44
00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.232
"Thank you, Beth.

45
00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.461
You are too kind and I'm going to miss you terribly.

46
00:03:23.481 --> 00:03:26.763
I really am," Amy said, hugging her tightly.

47
00:03:27.903 --> 00:03:29.084
"Have you packed away Mr.

48
00:03:29.124 --> 00:03:31.865
Huggie?" Jo called out loudly as she walked in.

49
00:03:32.785 --> 00:03:36.947
Mr. Huggie was an old stuffed animal that Amy used to sleep with when she was a little

50
00:03:36.987 --> 00:03:43.970
girl. "Unfortunately there is no room for him in my suitcase," Amy said, pointing to her oversized luggage.

51
00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.612
"But he's going to miss you," Jo teased.

52
00:03:48.456 --> 00:03:51.898
"I feel better knowing he's here with you," Amy said in return.

53
00:03:53.038 --> 00:03:57.340
After Aunt March announced that she was taking Amy with her, it put a strain on Jo and

54
00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.380
Amy's relationship.

55
00:03:59.261 --> 00:04:05.123
Jo wasn't angry, but under the circumstances, she found it hard, as anyone would, not to be resentful.

56
00:04:06.224 --> 00:04:10.325
Now, however, it appeared that the tension had lifted and life was back to normal.

57
00:04:11.226 --> 00:04:16.328
"You deserve to go, Amy, and I hope you have the time of your life," Jo said sincerely.

58
00:04:17.176 --> 00:04:18.257
"Do you mean that, Jo?"

59
00:04:18.637 --> 00:04:19.137
asked Amy.

60
00:04:19.157 --> 00:04:23.760
"Yes, and I'm sorry for behaving immaturely," begged Jo.

61
00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.421
"Will you forgive me?"

62
00:04:26.322 --> 00:04:30.344
Amy hugged her sister hard and cried, "Oh, Jo, there's nothing to forgive.

63
00:04:30.885 --> 00:04:32.966
I'm just relieved that you aren't upset at me.

64
00:04:32.986 --> 00:04:37.969
I'll write as often as I can and tell you all about the places I see and the

65
00:04:38.029 --> 00:04:38.810
people I meet."

66
00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:40.351
"I'd like that, Amy.

67
00:04:40.571 --> 00:04:43.572
I really would," said Jo.

68
00:04:43.592 --> 00:04:49.214
Having accepted that she might never have a chance to visit Europe in her lifetime, Jo was busying

69
00:04:49.254 --> 00:04:53.855
her days with writing, but she could not shake a restlessness that had developed in her heart.

70
00:04:54.975 --> 00:04:59.636
Lying in the yard one afternoon, Jo looked up at the sky and saw a couple of birds

71
00:04:59.697 --> 00:05:00.417
swirling around.

72
00:05:00.437 --> 00:05:06.538
"I wish I could spread my wings and fly off like you," she said to them dreamily.

73
00:05:07.819 --> 00:05:12.080
The dark shadow of a human face blocked her view just then, disrupting her daydream.

74
00:05:13.064 --> 00:05:16.266
"If you had wings, how would anybody be able to catch you?"

75
00:05:16.566 --> 00:05:20.568
the face said, showing that he had clearly been listening to her private monologue.

76
00:05:21.189 --> 00:05:25.631
"The whole point is never to be caught but to have the freedom to go wherever you choose,"

77
00:05:25.911 --> 00:05:26.552
Jo replied.

78
00:05:26.572 --> 00:05:30.854
"And how rude of you to sneak up on an unsuspecting person."

79
00:05:31.735 --> 00:05:36.437
Reaching out to the hand extended toward her, Jo sat up and grinned into the face of her

80
00:05:36.497 --> 00:05:37.098
best friend.

81
00:05:37.118 --> 00:05:39.999
"What are you doing home at this time of the week?"

82
00:05:40.319 --> 00:05:41.744
she asked Laurie.

83
00:05:41.764 --> 00:05:43.665
He shrugged and changed the subject instead.

84
00:05:44.065 --> 00:05:46.246
"I hear Amy's off to Europe with your old aunt."

85
00:05:47.206 --> 00:05:47.807
"That's right.

86
00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:49.327
She's going for one year.

87
00:05:49.808 --> 00:05:50.748
Now back to you.

88
00:05:51.368 --> 00:05:52.269
Why are you home?"

89
00:05:52.729 --> 00:05:55.310
Jo smartly brought the conversation back to Laurie.

90
00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:58.971
"I've been suspended," Laurie finally admitted.

91
00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:01.913
"Why? Laurie, what happened?"

92
00:06:02.253 --> 00:06:03.874
Jo asked in an alarmed voice.

93
00:06:03.894 --> 00:06:09.276
"I got in a fight with these guys and well here I am," he said lightly.

94
00:06:10.176 --> 00:06:11.697
"How long are you suspended for?"

95
00:06:11.957 --> 00:06:12.478
Jo asked.

96
00:06:12.498 --> 00:06:15.220
"Maybe two weeks," Laurie replied.

97
00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:21.444
Jo gazed at him with concern knowing that he was going to college to please his grandfather, but

98
00:06:21.484 --> 00:06:23.586
he hadn't quite adapted to the life there.

99
00:06:24.286 --> 00:06:26.548
She wanted to scold him but something stopped her.

100
00:06:28.109 --> 00:06:34.253
Instead she said, "Well, I'm glad you're here because after Amy leaves tomorrow, I'm going to be so

101
00:06:34.413 --> 00:06:37.676
miserable. You can be a good boy and get me through this."

102
00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:42.323
Grinning mischievously, Laurie saluted her and said, "Yes, sir!

103
00:06:42.943 --> 00:06:44.684
I live to carry out your orders."

104
00:06:46.986 --> 00:06:52.770
The next day bright and early, after Amy managed to fit all her suitcases, paint sets, easel, and

105
00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:57.533
other art supplies into Aunt March's carriage, she said her farewells to her family.

106
00:06:57.553 --> 00:06:58.894
"Good-bye, everyone!

107
00:06:59.534 --> 00:07:03.517
I'll miss you all very much," she cried out, giving each person a hug.

108
00:07:03.537 --> 00:07:07.880
"Be careful not to catch a cold," Mother said tearfully.

109
00:07:08.884 --> 00:07:11.145
"Remember to write often," said her father.

110
00:07:11.165 --> 00:07:15.967
"Find yourself a handsome Italian prince," were Jo's parting words.

111
00:07:15.987 --> 00:07:21.369
"Please think of us because we'll be thinking of you," pleaded Beth.

112
00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:24.791
"Take care of yourself," cried Meg and John.

113
00:07:24.811 --> 00:07:28.672
"I may make a surprise visit on you," Laurie called out.

114
00:07:28.692 --> 00:07:30.853
"That would be wonderful, Laurie.

115
00:07:31.133 --> 00:07:32.234
I do hope you'll come.

116
00:07:33.014 --> 00:07:34.574
Bye! Good-bye!"

117
00:07:35.175 --> 00:07:38.076
Amy shouted, as the carriage disappeared around the corner.
